  "limitations": [
    "Review-only local PG73 plus proposals; no formal migration, remote SQL, Worker, Provider or production credential changed.",
    "The fixture installs full v351, v353/v354, v356/v357/v359/v360/v361/v362/v365/v366/v367 proposals, the exact v368 held writer and counter policy, v371/v372/v376 successors, real v2 economic producer and receipt, and v347/v348/v349 buyer-login split. v374 is tested as an incompatible negative control.",
    "The v376 ACL is a reviewed proposal, not a formal production migration. Its coverage is limited to the v372 opt-in buyer branch.",
    "Legacy shared-key buyer holds are seeded by the privileged migrator in one transaction; the installed v2 deferred trigger verifies each account/hold receipt. This does not establish a v361-to-shared-key admission path or production role routing.",
    "One direct v351 Guardrail reserve/dispatch is checked before v361 revokes its direct entry; the deployed v361 wrapper and the later production Guardrail admission switch are not exercised.",
    "The buyer log amount and usage evidence are caller supplied; no immutable final result or independently authenticated Provider bill binds the debit.",
    "The audit snapshot is derived from the locked database account and settled hold. This fixture checks two same-user requests with separate API keys and caller pre-state corruption, but production-scale contention remains unmeasured.",
    "The global SHARE ROW EXCLUSIVE window-table lock serializes all writers and may cause capacity loss or deadlock retries. Production-scale contention remains unmeasured.",
    "Only the narrow non-grant, current-epoch, charged-basis held actual/v2 path is covered. Reserved, old-epoch, late actual, BYOK, recovery, no-hold and commit-unknown replay need successors."
